{"id": "EUVD-2026-85423", "enisaUuid": "0e966550-1463-3661-afdc-fe2ae5514453", "description": "In Flatpak before 1.18.1, a malicious sandboxed app can replace ~/.var/app/$appid/.ld.so with a symlink, causing regenerate_ld_cache to write files at an arbitrary location. The filenames and content are not attacker controlled, making this hard to exploit.", "datePublished": "2026-09-23T16:54:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-26T22:51:21", "baseScore": 4.0, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:L", "references": ["https://github.com/flatpak/flatpak/security/advisories/GHSA-99wv-m8rp-g58x"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-96807"], "assigner": "mitre", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b23c7638-ea75-3cb4-ba01-55339fbca717", "product": {"name": "flatpak", "vendor": {"name": "flatpak"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.18.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2f001f49-6579-317c-a09f-ddc40f7cce59", "vendor": {"name": "flatpak"}}], "isExploited": false}